{"c":[{"id":"fcf84ccb0d6c698f","sum":"DF1: acceptance debug socket needs --test-hooks or CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; uninstall.sh leaves the dev.caret.host Metal cache. Store build strips the manifest key (ID differs from EXTENSION_ID). FigureView freezes when rendersOffscreen; FigureIdle uses figureLife.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c55d146fc1f7fbe5","sum":"DF1: acceptance builds answer all debug-socket commands only with --test-hooks or CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full (since e0d39205), else state and spend only. kit uninstall.sh leaves $(getconf DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR)dev.caret.host (Metal shader cache) behind.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T045910Z-0e9f96548471c298","text":"Acceptance builds (build-app.sh acceptance) answer every debug-socket command only with --test-hooks or CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full since e0d39205; otherwise state and spend only, as a release build (DF1).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T045910Z-abba01c47d6ec6b1","text":"kit uninstall.sh leaves $(getconf DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR)dev.caret.host (a Metal shader cache) behind; DF1's VM run 20261009T044644Z-88912 found it after uninstall.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f1360355f32207bc","sum":"Store build (pnpm build:store) strips the manifest key, so its ID differs from extension/EXTENSION_ID; tabs permission dropped (host permissions expose title/url). FigureView freezes when rendersOffscreen; FigureIdle randomness from figureLife, glance from figureTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T065942Z-e248ff8cee60b01f","text":"Caret for Chrome store build (pnpm build:store) strips the manifest key, so the store ID differs from extension/EXTENSION_ID until the store's public key replaces it; tabs was dropped because the http(s) host permissions already expose tab title/url (checked in Chromium).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T082841Z-10e03653f161cdd3","text":"FigureView freezes itself when rendersOffscreen is set (Gallery.png), so references never catch a rest blink; rest beats (FigureIdle) take randomness from the figureLife environment (.seeded/.frozen) and the slip's glance direction from figureTyping, set in SurfaceCoordinator.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f74980d9c0267697","sum":"CI off v2/access needs a carrier commit with v2.yml/record-snapshots.yml (sam/v2/ci) on a v2/** branch. rig-run memory file 4-12 GiB (Gemma needs >4). macOS 26 guest: system-wide AX focused element fails; falls back to frontmost app. Copy run dirs before caret-heavy prune.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"21e9ae58ea94a1ed","sum":"v2/access lacks .github/workflows/v2.yml and record-snapshots.yml (on sam/v2/ci with Swift 6.3 perch fixes); CI off v2/access needs a carrier commit on a v2/** branch. rig-run takes a memory file (4-12 GiB); Gemma 3.4 GB runs out of GPU memory at 4 GiB.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T082841Z-f6fa2a2274a3373e","text":"v2/access (2026-10-09) has no .github/workflows/v2.yml or record-snapshots.yml; those live on sam/v2/ci with Swift 6.3 perch fixes, so CI for a branch off v2/access needs a carrier commit with them pushed to a v2/** branch (and snapshots/record).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T094824Z-62ada46022b5500b","text":"rig-run takes an opt-in memory file (whole GiB, 4-12) beside display; ops/heavy seals it (c0afa4d1). The 3.4 GB Gemma model runs out of GPU memory at the default 4 GiB.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"06b7217beca7b83b","sum":"macOS 26 rig guest: system-wide AX element answers -25204 for focused element/app, the app's own element works; AXRead.focusedElement falls back to the frontmost app. caret-heavy prune deletes inputs/vm-job/runs; copy run dirs out before pruning an r2-vm job.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261009T094824Z-d932ee9a36702a5a","text":"In the macOS 26 rig guest the system-wide AX element answers -25204 for its focused element and app while the app's own element works; AXRead.focusedElement falls back to the frontmost app (DF1 run 20261009T091737Z-83186).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261009T094824Z-f579be04c067ac3a","text":"caret-heavy prune deletes inputs/vm-job/runs (the whole guest evidence); copy the run directory out before pruning an r2-vm job.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
